api_contract_examples:
Endpoint surface (HTTP + SDK):

1) POST /v1/optimize/recommendations/prepare
   - Body: { "recommendation_id": "<rid>", "target": "project:route", "config_changes": [ ... ], "dry_run": boolean }
   - Headers: Authorization, Idempotency-Key(optional)
   - Response: 202 Accepted with { "apply_token": "token-abc", "preview_url": "https://console/...", "est_cost_savings": "120.5" }

2) POST /v1/optimize/recommendations/confirm
   - Body: { "apply_token": "token-abc", "confirm_mode": "commit" }
   - Headers: Authorization, Idempotency-Key(required)
   - Response: 200 OK { "status": "applied", "change_id": "chg-20250303-01" }

3) POST /v1/optimize/recommendations/cancel
   - Body: { "apply_token": "token-abc" }
   - Response: 200 OK { "status": "canceled" }

4) GET /v1/optimize/changes/{change_id}/status
   - Response: 200 OK { "status": "applied|failed|rolling_back", "events": [ ... ] }

Idempotency semantics: server stores Idempotency-Key -> outcome mapping for 24h. If request with same Idempotency-Key and same payload is received, server returns the stored outcome. If payload differs, return 409 Conflict. The apply_token is single-use for confirm/cancel and expires after TTL (default 15m).
